{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"**Changes Made**\n\n- Updated `bot.py` → `build_system`:\n  - Split the system prompt into **two separate cacheable blocks**.\n  - **Block 1** contains the immutable `INSTRUCTIONS` and is marked `ephemeral`.\n  - **Block 2** holds the per‑athlete, per‑day context (`athlete_context`) and is also marked `ephemeral`.\n  - Added a detailed docstring explaining the two‑block strategy.\n\n**Applied Parts of the Colleague’s Note**\n\n- **Two `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` markers** – implemented exactly as suggested, separating static instructions from volatile context.\n- Ensured the **static instructions block stays byte‑identical** across users and calls, allowing the Anthropic cache to retain the prefix.\n- Placed **all mutable data (date, profile, facts, language)** in the second block so that only this tail is regenerated on each `save_fact` write."}}
